A problem statement is a clear description of a specific issue that requires investigation. In the field of information technology, this often involves a technological system or process that fails to meet user needs. Research examines such systems to identify gaps and propose solutions that address these shortcomings. Without a well-defined problem statement, researchers risk pursuing unfocused inquiries or developing solutions that do not effectively resolve the existing issues (McCombes & George, 2023; Johnson, 2018).
