A problem statement is the most important part of any research or issue under study. It identifies exactly what problem needs to be addressed, thereby preventing wasted effort on irrelevant areas. By describing what is missing in the current system, researchers can more easily identify gaps that require attention. Furthermore, a clear problem statement helps researchers design appropriate methods to study the problem and select the right tools to solve it. In the field of information technology, a well-defined problem statement enables research to address real-world challenges faced by users, organizations, and industries (McCombes & George, 2023; Johnson, 2018; Purdue OWL, n.d.).

